Debian setup
============

1. Install and edit the configuration:

     sudo install -o root -g dns-zone-publisher -m 0640 \
       /usr/share/doc/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/examples/publisher.toml \
       /etc/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/publisher.toml
     sudoedit /etc/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/publisher.toml

2. Install credentials. Replace /path/to with your source directory and use
   your signing-key basename in both these commands and publisher.toml:

     sudo install -d -o root -g dns-zone-publisher -m 0750 \
       /etc/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/credentials \
       /etc/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/keys
     sudo install -o root -g dns-zone-publisher -m 0640 \
       /path/to/netbox-token /etc/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/credentials/
     sudo install -o root -g dns-zone-publisher -m 0640 \
       /path/to/Kexample.com.+013+12345.key \
       /path/to/Kexample.com.+013+12345.private \
       /etc/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/keys/

   For SSH targets, generate a key on the publisher and install verified host keys:

     sudo install -d -o dns-zone-publisher -g dns-zone-publisher -m 0700 \
       /var/lib/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/.ssh
     sudo -u dns-zone-publisher ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -N '' \
       -f /var/lib/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/.ssh/id_ed25519
     sudo install -o dns-zone-publisher -g dns-zone-publisher -m 0600 \
       /path/to/known_hosts /var/lib/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/.ssh/known_hosts
     sudo cat /var/lib/netbox-dns-zone-publisher/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

   Copy the generated public key to each target. For a receiving account named
   dns-publish with home /var/lib/dns-publish, run there:

     sudo install -d -o dns-publish -g dns-publish -m 0700 /var/lib/dns-publish/.ssh
     sudo install -o dns-publish -g dns-publish -m 0600 \
       /path/to/id_ed25519.pub /var/lib/dns-publish/.ssh/authorized_keys

3. Create local target directories. Give dns-zone-publisher write access and
   the DNS server read access. Add each target to the service's writable paths:

     sudo systemctl edit netbox-dns-zone-publisher.service

     [Service]
     ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/coredns/zones

4. Check that the initial UTC YYYYMMDD01 serial exceeds the deployed SOA serial.
   Run once, inspect the logs, then enable the timer:

     sudo systemctl start netbox-dns-zone-publisher.service
     sudo journalctl -u netbox-dns-zone-publisher.service
     sudo systemctl enable --now netbox-dns-zone-publisher.timer
